  era: "c. 2600\u20131900 BCE \xB7 Section 2 \xB7 Indus Valley Civilisation \xB7 c. 3300 \u2013 1300 BCE (mature phase c. 2600 \u2013 1900 BCE)"
  title: Harappan technology
  text: Harappans worked copper and bronze, made glazed faience, drilled long carnelian beads with special drills, and fired bricks in kilns. Lothal had a large brick basin often interpreted as a dockyard, though some scholars see it as a reservoir.
